00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:22,000
然后全凭你一句话决定
他们到底是赢，
还是输得惨绝人寰。
Then at the end you can decide
whether they win or they lose,
really badly.

283
00:14:22,033 --> 00:14:23,367
我挺喜欢树叶桂冠这主意。
I like the leaves.

284
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:25,200
-我就知道你喜欢。
-我倒没想过树叶这茬。
-I thought you might.
-I hadn't thought
of the leaves.

285
00:14:25,233 --> 00:14:29,600
要是我，就冲舒马赫演得跟坏蛋皮埃尔一样绝，
直接给他打100分，
齐活了！
I'd have given Schumacher 100
for being Dick Dastardly,
there we are!

286
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:33,600
-咱们能翻篇了吗？
我担心压力太大了。
-不行，我还有个主意。
-Can we move on?
I'm worried about the stress.
-No, I've another idea.

287
00:14:33,633 --> 00:14:35,633
你知道谢菲尔德夜店里那些人吧，
You know people in Sheffield
nightclubs,

288
00:14:35,667 --> 00:14:37,500
总爱在旁边拱火，
撺掇哥们儿去干架。
they're always
egging their mates
to have a fight.

289
00:14:37,533 --> 00:14:40,867
-没错。
-所有车队的维修区P房里
都该配这么一个人。
-Yes.
-All of those pit garages
should have one of those.

290
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:43,567
“看见那个阿隆索没？
他刚才直勾勾盯着你的指示牌看呢。”
See that Alonso?
He were looking
at your pit board.

291
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,700
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

292
00:14:46,733 --> 00:14:49,533
“他把你练习赛的圈速给搅黄了，
你打算怎么着？
你总不能当缩头乌龟吧！”
He spilt your practice lap,
what you gonna do?
You can't do nothin'.

293
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:53,033
绝对精彩绝伦。
听着，伯尼，你要是在看电视的话，
It'd be brilliant.
Listen, Bernie,
if you're watching,

294
00:14:53,067 --> 00:14:55,800
你有我的电话，
给我打过来，
顺便带点树叶。
you've got my number,
give me a call
and some leaves.

295
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,367
这差事非我莫属。
I'm your man.

296
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,767
-接下来聊聊今年最酷的一台车。
-啥车？
-On now to one of the coolest
cars of the year.
-What?

297
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:03,200
是一台福特MPV保姆车。
It is a Ford people carrier.

298
00:15:03,233 --> 00:15:05,367
就是这台，瞧瞧！
There it is, look!

299
00:15:05,367 --> 00:15:07,933
克拉克森：你还记得上周
你开我那辆奔驰时撞到脑袋了吧。
CLARKSON: You know last week,
you banged your head while
you were driving my Mercedes.

300
00:15:07,967 --> 00:15:09,367
记得啊。
Yes.

301
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,633
-脑子撞坏了？
-没有，说正经的，
听我把话说完。
-Has this?
-No, no, seriously.
Bear with me.

302
00:15:11,667 --> 00:15:16,167
首先，
它虽然是一台七座MPV，
但长得那是真帅！
For one thing,
it's a seven-seater MPV,
but it's really cool looking!

303
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,567
这车确实棒。
It's a great car.

304
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,800
他说得一点没错，
我买了一台，而我是个单身汉。
He's absolutely right,
I have it, and I'm a bachelor.

305
00:15:19,833 --> 00:15:21,667
开起来真的很爽，而且……
It drives really well and...

306
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,367
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

307
00:15:24,367 --> 00:15:26,600
我的意思是，
纯粹作为一辆车我很喜欢它。
What I mean is,
I like it as a car.

308
00:15:26,633 --> 00:15:28,467
我用不着去想……
后排座椅还能旋转，
I don't have to think...
The seats swivel,

309
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:31,000
后边能塞下一大堆
花花绿绿的
Mothercare母婴地垫。
I can get a lot
of brightly coloured
Mothercare rugs in the back.

310
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:34,633
你正好能拿你的小毛刷
去刷空调出风口了，詹姆斯。
You can just have
your little brush for cleaning
the air vents, James.

311
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:38,133
詹姆斯·梅大谈育儿经：
“花花绿绿的
Mothercare……”
James May on parenting.
"Brightly coloured
Mothercare..."

312
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:42,833
不管怎么说，它用的是小钢炮福克斯ST
那台2.5升
五缸发动机，
Anyway, you get that 2.5L,
five cylinder engine
from the fast Focus ST,

313
00:15:42,867 --> 00:15:47,067
所以声浪动听极了，
跑得快，操控好，
简直酷毙了。
so it sounds brilliant,
it's fast, it handles well,
it's a cool car.

314
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:51,067
所以你的意思是，
万一你避孕套破了，
这下也不叫事儿了。
What you're saying then
is if your condom bursts,
it's not a problem any more.

315
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,533
没毛病，
这就是标准答案。
There you go,
there's your answer.

316
00:15:52,567 --> 00:15:54,533
那么，通常情况下……
Now, ordinarily...

317
00:15:54,567 --> 00:16:00,467
通常情况下，我是绝不会给这两个货
参演的任何节目
打广告的，懂吧？
Ordinarily, I wouldn't plug
any show that these
two are appearing in, okay?

318
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:05,967
但詹姆斯最近签约主持了
天空台32频道的节目，行吧？
But James has recently
signed up to host
a programme on Sky 32, okay?

319
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,900
-叫《当鲨鱼发起攻击》。
-没错。
-Called When Sharks Attack.
-Yeah.

320
00:16:08,933 --> 00:16:10,433
这节目还真挺值得一看，
Now, this is worth watching,

321
00:16:10,467 --> 00:16:13,367
因为我好不容易搞到了
一张剧照，
because I've managed
to procure a still,

322
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,533
出自詹姆斯的节目，
就是这张。
from the production of James
and here it is.

323
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:18,633
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

324
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:23,667
克拉克森：这节目
你绝对不能错过。
CLARKSON: This is a show
you cannot miss.

325
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:27,133
哈蒙德：这在咱们国家
合法吗？
HAMMOND: Is that legal
in this country?

326
00:16:27,167 --> 00:16:30,833
瞧瞧这芭比娃娃效果，
肯和芭比那裤裆，
It's the Barbie doll
thing here,
the Ken and Barbie crotch,

327
00:16:30,867 --> 00:16:32,600
平平整整，啥动静也没有。
there's nothing happening.

328
00:16:33,467 --> 00:16:35,700
我不知道
你们有什么好笑的。
I don't know
why you're laughing.

329
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:37,567
等等！我最近可没干
什么蠢事。
Hang on! I haven't done
anything silly lately.

330
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,467
上周报纸上有张照片，
There was a picture
in the paper last week,

331
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,533
我这儿正巧有，
是你那个圣杯节目的。
which I've got,
on your Grail programme.

332
00:16:41,567 --> 00:16:44,233
就是那张宣传照，
来了！
The publicity shot,
here it is!

333
00:16:44,267 --> 00:16:46,733
那匹马到底是有多小啊？
How small was that horse?

334
00:16:47,867 --> 00:16:49,233
（怪笑）那其实是……
(CACKLING) It was...

335
00:16:49,267 --> 00:16:51,900
理查德问：“你是骑了匹
小马宝莉吗？”
Richard says, "Have you got
a My Little Pony?"

336
00:16:51,933 --> 00:16:54,967
我看了看心想：
“老子骑上去之后，
马不都长这样么。”
I looked at it and thought,
"That's what horses look like
when I get on them."

337
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,033
所以，鬼知道那到底算个啥。
So, God knows what that was.

338
00:16:57,067 --> 00:16:59,400
行了，
新闻环节就到这里。
Anyway,
that is the end of the news.

339
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:02,200
现在言归正传。
大家还记得去年吗？
Now, we must move on.
You remember last year?

340
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:05,000
我飞去加利福尼亚，
开着一辆本田NSX
在赛道上狂飙。
I went out to California
and drove a Honda NSX
round a race track.

341
00:17:05,033 --> 00:17:08,767
是为了挑战我在PlayStation游戏里
跑出的圈速成绩。
It was to do with racing
a time I'd set
on a PlayStation game.

342
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,133
问题是，
我跑了个1分58秒，对吧？
The thing was,
I did it in 1minute 58, okay?

343
00:17:12,167 --> 00:17:14,467
跑了两三圈后，
成绩就到了1分58秒，
After a couple of laps,
I got to 1minute 58,

344
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:18,667
可之后不管我再跑多少圈，
都快不了一丁点了。
and then no matter
how many times I went round,
I couldn't go any faster.

345
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:22,133
那已经是我的天赋
和胆量极限了。
It was my limit of talent
and bravery.

346
00:17:22,167 --> 00:17:25,933
在杰里米那番坦白说毫无卵用的挣扎
被公之于电视屏幕之后，
And after Jeremy's frankly
useless efforts were
put on the television,

347
00:17:25,967 --> 00:17:30,100
一位名叫杰基·斯图尔特的
苏格兰大妈给我们写了封信，说……
a Scottish lady
called Jackie Stewart
wrote to us, saying...

348
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,967
她能让我们当中的任何一个人，
She could get any one of us

349
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,633
开任何车去全国任何一条赛道，
先做出自己的最快圈速，
to any race track
in the country in any car,
get us to set our best time

350
00:17:36,667 --> 00:17:40,633
然后她能帮我们
把成绩削掉整整20秒。
and then she could get us
to knock 20 seconds
off that time.

351
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:42,700
“他”。人家是男的。
He. It's a he.

352
00:17:42,733 --> 00:17:43,900
杰基·斯图尔特是个老爷们儿。
Jackie Stewart's a he.

353
00:17:44,633 --> 00:17:46,633
好吧。
Righto.

354
00:17:46,667 --> 00:17:50,433
无论如何，
重点是我们决定接受他的挑战，
Anyway,
the point is we decided
to accept his challenge,

355
00:17:50,467 --> 00:17:54,467
只是，我们挑了所有人里
最难教的一个学生交给他。
only we gave him
the most difficult pupil
of them all.

356
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,733
就是他！
Him!

357
00:17:55,767 --> 00:17:57,400
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

358
00:18:04,767 --> 00:18:07,700
大家可以看到，
我正身处一个极其陌生的环境。
You find me
in unfamiliar surroundings.

359
00:18:10,167 --> 00:18:12,133
这是一条赛道。
This is a race track.

360
00:18:12,167 --> 00:18:15,567
这是装我提速战袍的包，
This is my bag of
go-faster clothing,

361
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:18,833
我来这里是为了赴一场
与杰基爵士的约会。
and I'm here for my date
with Sir Jackie.

362
00:18:20,067 --> 00:18:21,633
梅：他来了，
MAY: And here he is,

363
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:24,600
带着赛车手标志性的
“低调”方式登场。
making a typically understated
racing driver's entrance.

364
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,200
杰基·斯图尔特是个传奇人物。
Jackie Stewart is a legend.

365
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:35,967
跻身于屈指可数的顶尖车手行列，
曾三度夺得F1世界冠军。
One of that elite band of drivers who have
won the F1 World Championship 3 times.

366
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,533
而且，我瞎猜的啊，我觉得他
还挺为自己是苏格兰人而自豪的。
And, and I'm guessing here, I think he's
also proud of being Scottish.

367
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:46,067
一见面，
我就让这位“麦克传奇”
心里有个数。
Immediately,
I let the McLegend
know what he was in for.

368
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,633
你知道他们
都叫我“龟速船长”吧。
You know they
call me Captain Slow.

369
00:18:47,667 --> 00:18:49,067
-是吗？
-对啊。
-Do they?
-Yeah.

370
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:52,367
嗯，我见过那个大块头开车，
猛得很。
Well, I've seen the bigger guy
drive very aggressively.

371
00:18:52,367 --> 00:18:54,133
呃，而且开得也不怎么样，
我觉得。
Mmm, and not very well,
I thought.

372
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:55,467
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLES)

373
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:57,100
那么，你觉得
能教得会我吗？
So, do you think
you can do it?

374
00:18:57,133 --> 00:19:00,000
以前没坐过你的车，
这不好说。
Never having driven
with you before,
it's difficult to say.

375
00:19:00,033 --> 00:19:04,667
不过你要是没开得
比另外那俩好，
我反而会觉得奇怪。
I'd be surprised if you
didn't turn out to be better
than the other two.

376
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:07,233
这话我爱听。
I like that.

377
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:08,700
对于这次特训，
For this coaching session,

378
00:19:08,733 --> 00:19:12,367
杰基坚持要选
一辆后驱车。
Jackie had insisted on
a rear wheel drive car.

379
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:18,067
于是我们挑了全新的
TVR Tuscan 2敞篷版，
So, we chose the new
TVR Tuscan 2 Convertible,

380
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:20,967
因为这车其实
正合我们的胃口。
because actually it's a car
we're very interested in.

381
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:26,100
首先，TVR坚称
这是他们迄今为止做工最好、
开起来最爽的车，
Firstly, because TVR claims
it's their best-built,
best-driving car till date,

382
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:29,233
其次，鉴于他们
目前面临的重重经营危机，
and secondly, with all their
present business problems,

383
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:32,100
这很有可能是
该公司的绝唱了。
it could well be
the company's swan song.

384
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:38,767
在上课前，
杰基先把TVR开出去
刷了个他自己的圈速。
Before school began,
Jackie took the TVR out
to set his own lap time.

385
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,167
我已经开始发慌了。
I'm scared already.

386
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:43,400
杰基·斯图尔特已经66岁了，
是个退休领养老金的老头，
Jackie Stewart is 66,
a pensioner,

387
00:19:43,433 --> 00:19:45,900
只不过好像
没人告诉过他这点。
except no-one seems
to have told him that.

388
00:19:45,933 --> 00:19:47,567
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINE ROARING)

389
00:19:48,933 --> 00:19:50,433
这下胎算是热开了。
That warmed the tyres up.

390
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:56,233
杰基·斯图尔特：冲上坡顶，
轻带刹车。
JACKIE STEWART: Over the top
and lightly brake.

391
00:19:57,133 --> 00:20:00,767
轻柔地重新给油。
Gently get back on the power.

392
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:04,133
全油门，收油，
降入二挡。
Full power, off the power,
down into second.

393
00:20:04,967 --> 00:20:06,767
让车顺势滑进弯。
Let it roll in.

394
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,733
跑在上面，这赛道的大半段
你根本都看不见盲区。
You can't see
half of this track,
as you're going along it.

395
00:20:09,767 --> 00:20:12,633
没错，我知道，这就是它
迷人的地方之一。
No, I know. That's one of the
charming things about it.

396
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:14,867
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINE ROARING)

397
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:19,667
好嘞。
Right.

398
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:22,733
杰基·斯图尔特爵士，
你的用时是……
Sir Jackie Stewart,
you did it in...

399
00:20:22,767 --> 00:20:26,000
1分58秒9。
One minute, 58.9.

400
00:20:26,033 --> 00:20:27,967
现在，轮到我了。
Now it was my turn.

401
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,767
最要紧的是，
一开始千万别急，慢慢来。
The main thing to do is take
your time to begin with.

402
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:33,300
我怕是直到今天收工，
都还在“慢慢来”呢！
I might still
be taking my time
at the end of the day!

403
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:36,033
走着瞧吧。
Let's wait and see.

404
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:38,700
梅：刚开始跑的那几圈，
杰基就像《超级保姆》里的育儿专家一样，
MAY: For my first few laps,
Jackie, like Supernanny,

405
00:20:38,733 --> 00:20:41,000
一言不发，
只在一旁冷眼旁观。
said nothing
and just observed.

406
00:20:41,033 --> 00:20:45,667
与此同时，他的比赛工程师
通过车内遥测数据
死死盯着我的圈速。
Meanwhile, his race engineer
monitored my times
using the in-car telemetry.

407
00:20:46,733 --> 00:20:48,967
我的最好成绩惨不忍睹。
My best time was poor.

408
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,300
斯图尔特：
2分26秒。
STEWART:
Two minutes, 26 seconds.

409
00:20:51,767 --> 00:20:52,800
真见鬼！
Sod it!

410
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,567
加把劲啊！
Come on!

411
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:57,267
可无论我怎么折腾，
成绩就是提不上去。
No matter what I did,
I couldn't improve it.

412
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,600
斯图尔特：你在这儿
路不够用了。
STEWART: You're gonna go
short of room here.

413
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:02,133
看来我是撞上了
所谓的天赋天花板，
It seemed I'd hit
my talent wall,

414
00:21:02,167 --> 00:21:06,167
就像杰里米当年
在拉古纳塞卡赛道一样。
just as Jeremy did
at Laguna Seca.

415
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:12,100
杰基定下的把圈速砍掉20秒的目标，
看起来根本就是天方夜谭。
Jackie's target of knocking
my time down by 20 seconds
looked impossible.

416
00:21:12,133 --> 00:21:14,367
尽管如此，他还是开始动手调教我了。
Nevertheless, he set to work.

417
00:21:14,367 --> 00:21:16,833
我觉得你脑子里可能在想太多
I think maybe you're trying
to think too much

418
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:21,133
自己当下是怎么开的，
而不是接下来该怎么开。
about how you're doing,
rather than what's coming up.

419
00:21:21,167 --> 00:21:25,433
出弯的路线，
可比入弯重要得多，
The exit of the corner,
is far more important
than the entry of the corner,

420
00:21:26,233 --> 00:21:27,633
尤其是平顺性方面。
with regards to smoothness.

421
00:21:27,667 --> 00:21:30,800
最核心的秘诀之一就是，
绝不要踩下油门踏板，
One of the big keys is
you never press the gas pedal

422
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:33,633
除非你确定踩下去后就不用再松开。
until you know you never
have to take it off.

423
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,533
明白。
Right.

424
00:21:35,567 --> 00:21:37,467
换句话说，
很多人一脚油门跺下去，
In other words,
lots of people
stamp on the gas pedal,

425
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:41,033
以为能更快，
结果又松开、再踩、再松开，
thinking they'll go faster,
then they take it off,
put it on, take it off,

426
00:21:41,067 --> 00:21:43,367
最后才彻底踩死。
and finally get it on again.

427
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:44,800
你可千万别那么干。
You don't wanna do that.

428
00:21:47,133 --> 00:21:49,567
刚才那番谆谆教导听着还挺舒心的。
That was a nice soothing chat.

429
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:52,900
可一上了赛道，
这老爷子下达指令的方式可就凶狠多了。
On the track, though,
the man does like to make
his point.

430
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:54,767
斯图尔特：切进去，切，切，切！
STEWART: In, in, in, in.

431
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:56,700
切内道，进，进！
In, in, in.

432
00:21:56,733 --> 00:21:58,833
刹车，刹车，踩刹车！
Brake, brake, brake!

433
00:21:58,867 --> 00:22:00,567
刹车，带住刹车！
Brake, brake.

434
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:03,800
给油，再给点油，继续给！
More power, more power,
more power.

435
00:22:03,833 --> 00:22:06,800
全油门，全油门，踩到底！
Full power, full power,
full power.

436
00:22:06,833 --> 00:22:10,367
我要是下了地狱，
大概也就是这副惨状了：
This is probably what will
happen to me in hell.

437
00:22:10,367 --> 00:22:13,733
一辆TVR，一条赛道，
外加一个吹毛求疵的苏格兰老头。
A TVR, a race track
and a pedantic Scotsman.

438
00:22:13,767 --> 00:22:15,467
（斯图尔特笑声）
(STEWART LAUGHS)

439
00:22:16,767 --> 00:22:20,000
不过，多亏了他这套霸道又充满智慧的调教……
But, thanks to a mix
of bossiness and wisdom...

440
00:22:20,033 --> 00:22:21,933
提前降一挡！
Down a gear early.

441
00:22:21,967 --> 00:22:25,567
把准备动作都做完，
这样你才能专心在弯道里找速度。
Get all the work done,
so you can concentrate on
finding speed on the corner.

442
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,933
圈速开始一路狂降。
The lap time started
to tumble.

443
00:22:27,967 --> 00:22:29,833
2分23秒。
Two minutes 23 seconds.

444
00:22:29,867 --> 00:22:31,833
收油，刹车，降一挡。
Power off, brake, down a gear.

445
00:22:31,867 --> 00:22:33,367
脑子别乱，稳住。
Keep your head together.

446
00:22:33,367 --> 00:22:35,833
手上太忙活了，感觉车子反应不对劲了吧？
Too busy, you feel the car
responding badly?

447
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:37,633
切入弯心。切进去。
Turn it in. Turn it in.

448
00:22:37,667 --> 00:22:40,800
顺着顺出去。给油。全油门！
2分15秒。
Feed it out. Power on. Full!
2 minutes 15.

449
00:22:40,833 --> 00:22:44,667
到了下午中段，这位格子呢魔鬼教练
已经帮我砍掉了整整11秒，
By mid-afternoon the tartan
taskmaster had knocked
11 seconds,

450
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:49,033
比起我最初的成绩，
并大发慈悲准我歇会儿喝杯茶。
off my original
and allowed me a tea-break.

451
00:22:49,067 --> 00:22:52,633
在你们那个70年代，
我最喜欢的一点就是，
The thing I really like
about your era, the '70s,

452
00:22:52,667 --> 00:22:55,400
你们总是能把极限探得更远。
you just pushed the boundaries
a bit further.

453
00:22:55,433 --> 00:22:57,600
触碰到性能包线的边缘，
You got to the outside
of the envelope,

454
00:22:57,633 --> 00:23:00,200
我觉得比现在的人激进得多。
more than people do
these days, I think.

455
00:23:00,233 --> 00:23:03,400
那时候看着更直观，因为我们下压力小，
It was more obvious,
cause we had less down-force,

456
00:23:03,433 --> 00:23:06,767
气动效果没那么强，翼片也少，
车子滑得更厉害。
that's less aerodynamic,
fewer wings,
the car slid more.

457
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,967
呃，其实我说的主要是发型。
I was actually thinking more
in terms of the hairstyles.

458
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,467
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLES)

459
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,233
其实跟你现在这发型挺像的。
It's pretty close to what
you've got now, actually.

460
00:23:12,267 --> 00:23:13,833
难道真应了那句话……
Is it a case of...

461
00:23:13,867 --> 00:23:16,033
“长得像杰基·斯图尔特，
开得就跟杰基·斯图尔特一样快。”
"If you look like
Jackie Stewart, you'll go
like Jackie Stewart."

462
00:23:16,067 --> 00:23:18,367
你现在留这头发，就是冲着这个来的吧？
You're trying to do that now,
aren't you, with the hair?

463
00:23:18,367 --> 00:23:20,600
-我已经学到一半精髓了。
-（轻笑）
-I'm halfway there.
-(CHUCKLES)

464
00:23:20,633 --> 00:23:23,500
-再跑一圈，看看效果。
-好嘞。
-Let's have another go,
see what happens.
-Okay.

465
00:23:33,833 --> 00:23:36,367
咬住。全油门！
Stay with it. Full power!

466
00:23:36,367 --> 00:23:38,867
感觉到车子在晃了吧？我可不想看到这毛病。
You feel the car doing that,
I don't wanna feel that.

467
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:40,633
哎哟喂！
Whoops-a-daisy!

468
00:23:40,667 --> 00:23:43,367
除非你笃定不用再松油，
否则别急着踩死。
Don't put the power on
till you know you never
have to take it off.

469
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:44,367
很好。
Good.

470
00:23:44,367 --> 00:23:46,867
-2分10秒。漂亮。
-2分10秒？
-2:10. Yep.
-2:10?

471
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:50,800
杰基现在已经帮我狂砍了16秒，
Jackie had now slashed my time
by a massive 16 seconds,

472
00:23:50,833 --> 00:23:54,700
但哪怕再想快一丁点，都变得难如登天。
but any extra improvement
was getting harder and harder.

473
00:23:54,733 --> 00:23:58,167
你得集中精力。
你这圈看的刹车站牌跟刚才不一样了。
You've gotta concentrate.
You're not using the same
board as before.

474
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,733
脑子稳住。
Get your head together.

475
00:23:59,767 --> 00:24:02,600
看见没，你刚才离弯心起码偏了六英尺。
See, you missed that apex
probably by six feet.

476
00:24:03,067 --> 00:24:04,233
喔……
Whoa...

477
00:24:04,267 --> 00:24:06,833
踩油门。给油。踩下去。
Power on. On power. On power.

478
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:13,233
时间在一分一秒流逝，
而我们还得再抠出四秒来。
Time was running out
and we still had to find
another four seconds.

479
00:24:13,267 --> 00:24:15,833
于是，他把我叫回维修区
进行最后的战前动员。
So, he pulled me in
for a final pep talk.

480
00:24:15,867 --> 00:24:17,233
你刚才手上动作太碎了。
You're quite busy here.

481
00:24:17,267 --> 00:24:19,700
首先，我们对比了他和我的
遥测遥测数据图。
First, we compared his
and my telemetry.

482
00:24:19,733 --> 00:24:23,567
最上面显示的是：
红线是你跑的那圈，
蓝线是杰基跑的。
At the top we've got,
your lap is in red
and Jackie's is in blue.

483
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:25,800
而这两者的差距，
简直触目惊心。
And the differences
were alarming.

484
00:24:25,833 --> 00:24:29,367
斯图尔特：
你在这儿的加速，
看吧，多糙啊。
STEWART:
Your acceleration here,
you see how untidy it is.

485
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:31,367
呃，是不太完美。
Well, it's not perfect.

486
00:24:31,367 --> 00:24:35,700
这种指导，正是他平时
给现役F1车手
当教练时的拿手好戏。
This is something he does
when he coaches
current Formula One drivers.

487
00:24:35,733 --> 00:24:37,467
不过既然你都能教他们怎么开，
But if you can show them
how to do it,

488
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:39,900
那你干嘛不接着
开你的F1呢？
why don't you just carry on
being a Formula One driver?

489
00:24:39,933 --> 00:24:42,233
因为我早就
不想再干那个了。
Because I don't want
to be doing that any more.

490
00:24:42,267 --> 00:24:44,433
最后，他直接开启了
“尤达大师”玄学模式。
Finally he went
into Yoda mode.

491
00:24:44,467 --> 00:24:48,967
如果你正准备进弯，
而我突然这么推你一把，
瞧，你是不是直接栽倒了？
If you're going into a corner
and I do that to you,
look, you're falling over.

492
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,067
-但如果我这样慢慢顶你，
你就会顺势靠向我。
-没错。
-If I do that to you,
you lean into me.
-Yeah.

493
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:53,633
因为你心里有预期。
So you know it's gonna happen.

494
00:24:53,667 --> 00:24:55,800
车对你的反应，也是一模一样的道理。
The car reacts to you
in exactly the same way.

495
00:24:55,833 --> 00:24:59,433
就好像你从后面
接近一条恶犬，
It's like, if you walk up
behind a vicious dog,

496
00:24:59,467 --> 00:25:01,900
如果你一边走
一边跟它说话，
if you talk to the dog
on the way up,

497
00:25:01,933 --> 00:25:06,533
它就不会受惊，
也不会做出
任何出格的过激反应。
it won't be caught by surprise
and it won't do
something unpredictable.

498
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:08,533
还真是……显而易见的大实话。
Obvious, really.

499
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:16,267
留给杰基的时间只有刚满一小时，
他得帮我砍掉
最后这四秒，
Jackie had just over an hour
to shave off those
last four seconds

500
00:25:16,367 --> 00:25:19,000
把我带进2分06秒。
and get me down to 2:06.

501
00:25:19,033 --> 00:25:21,233
-冲啊！
-对，对，很好！
-Go for it!
-Yes, yes, that's good!

502
00:25:21,267 --> 00:25:22,933
再给油，再给油！
More power, more power.

503
00:25:22,967 --> 00:25:24,600
全油门！
回方向！
Full power.
Steer the angle off.

504
00:25:24,633 --> 00:25:28,467
往左打。漂亮。
这把比刚才好多了。
慢慢收油。
Steer left. Good.
Better this time.
Gently off the power.

505
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:29,800
给油！很好。
On power. Good.

506
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:32,133
-漂亮！
-不错，2分09秒。
-Yes!
-That's good. 2:09.

507
00:25:32,167 --> 00:25:34,767
大师的教诲，
我全都吸收了。
I'd absorbed all
the master's advice.

508
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:39,033
我现在只需要坚信一点：
这辆车，
真能像他说的那样跑得那么快！
I just needed to have faith
in the speeds he said,
the car could do.

509
00:25:39,067 --> 00:25:41,467
往那边去！开油！
Over there. Power on.

510
00:25:41,500 --> 00:25:44,267
差一点点。
再来一圈！全油门！
Not quite good enough.
One more lap. Full power.

511
00:25:44,367 --> 00:25:46,667
-漂亮！太棒了！
-好！非常棒！
-Yes! Yes!
-Good! Very good!

512
00:25:47,200 --> 00:25:48,967
打进弯心，打进去！
Turn it in, turn it in.

513
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,833
开油，回正，
回方向盘！很好！
Power on, angle off,
steering angle. Good.

514
00:25:50,867 --> 00:25:52,367
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLES)

515
00:25:52,367 --> 00:25:55,900
目前这圈很棒！稳住！
再往里切！甩出去！
Good lap so far. Keep going.
In more. Kick it out.

516
00:25:55,933 --> 00:25:57,400
全油门！踩到底！
Full power. Full!

517
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:02,233
你刚才跑了
2分06秒74！
You've just done
two minutes, 6.74.

518
00:26:02,767 --> 00:26:04,167
等等，让我再瞅一眼……
Hang on, let me just...

519
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,500
你做到了！
You've done it!

520
00:26:05,533 --> 00:26:06,633
-真的假的？！
-真跑到了！
-Have I?
-Yep.

521
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:08,133
你跑了6.7秒。
You've done 6.7.

522
00:26:09,033 --> 00:26:10,867
梅：太棒了！漂亮！我就知道！
MAY: Yes! Yes! I knew it!

523
00:26:15,533 --> 00:26:18,367
-（观众鼓掌）
-干得漂亮！干得好，伙计！
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)
-Well done! Well done, mate!

524
00:26:19,933 --> 00:26:21,533
相当快船长！
Captain Quite Fast!

525
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,700
我能……我能插一句吗，
Can I... Can I just say,

526
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:30,533
看刚才那段片子，
你全程几乎一句话都没说！
watching that,
you hardly spoke at all!

527
00:26:30,567 --> 00:26:32,867
啊！对，我正想
为这事道个歉来着。
Ah! Yes, I meant
to apologise for that.

528
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:36,100
问题是，
我当时太专注于
学怎么开车了，
The thing is,
I was concentrating
so hard on learning to drive,

529
00:26:36,133 --> 00:26:39,633
-我都忘了自己是个
电视节目主持人了。
-是啊，显而易见。
-I forgot that I was
a television presenter.
-Yes. Evidently.

530
00:26:39,667 --> 00:26:42,400
那你还记得
那台TVR开起来感觉怎么样吗？
Did you forget to remember
what the TVR was like?

531
00:26:42,433 --> 00:26:44,167
说实话，我还挺喜欢的。
Actually, I rather liked it.

532
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:46,100
换在以前，提到TVR，
你肯定会觉得：
In the old days, a TVR,
you'd have thought,

533
00:26:46,133 --> 00:26:48,833
“那是通往塑料死亡狂欢的
单程票！”
"That's a ticket to a festival
of plastic death!"

534
00:26:48,867 --> 00:26:51,700
但实际上，
我觉得它挺棒的，
而且操控极其出色。
Actually,
I thought it was good
and it handled really well.

535
00:26:51,733 --> 00:26:54,233
杰基·斯图尔特爵士也说
它操控很好。
Sir Jackie Stewart said
it handled well.

536
00:26:54,267 --> 00:26:56,733
-她真是个很有品位的女人！
-（轻笑）
-She's a discerning woman!
-(CHUCKLES)

537
00:26:56,767 --> 00:26:59,467
当然了，唯一的遗憾
就是那家工厂
快要倒闭停产了。
It's just a shame, of course,
that the factory's
closing down.

538
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:01,233
确实，这事儿我们能唠上一整天，
It is, we could dwell
on that for ages,

539
00:27:01,267 --> 00:27:05,067
但现在我们必须
把一位明星塞进我们崭新的
廉价车里了。
but we must now
put a star in our brand new
reasonably priced car.

540
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:06,900
今晚这位嘉宾
第一次来我们这儿时，
When our guest tonight
first came here,

541
00:27:06,933 --> 00:27:11,067
表现实在太过壮观，
以至于我们以他的名字
命名了一个弯道向他致敬。
he was so spectacular,
we named a corner
in his honour.

542
00:27:11,100 --> 00:27:14,800
女士们先生们，
掌声欢迎——
迈克尔·穿心弯爵士！
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome
Sir Michael Follow-through.

543
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:16,400
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

544
00:27:17,867 --> 00:27:19,867
-近来如何？
-还好吧？
-How are you?
-All right?

545
00:27:19,900 --> 00:27:21,700
-很高兴再次见到你。
-请坐！
-Good to see you again.
-Have a seat!

546
00:27:21,733 --> 00:27:23,700
迈克尔·甘本来了！
Michael Gambon is here!

547
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:26,200
哦。
Ooh.

548
00:27:28,833 --> 00:27:30,233
多纯爷们儿的汉子！
What a man!

549
00:27:31,867 --> 00:27:34,600
说实在的，我得坦白交代。
Now, I've gotta be honest.

550
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:38,367
我得说句实话，
你居然还会回来，
真让我挺吃惊的，
I've gotta be honest.
I'm very surprised
you came back,

551
00:27:38,367 --> 00:27:39,833
尤其在你上次来过之后。
after your last visit here.

552
00:27:39,867 --> 00:27:42,067
哎，我觉得我当时
可成功了啊。
Well, I thought I was
a huge success.

553
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:44,000
你？大获成功？！
You, a huge success!

554
00:27:44,033 --> 00:27:47,567
多亏了那个弯道——甘本弯，
我现在家喻户晓了，
人人都知道。
I'm a household name because
of that corner, Gambon Corner.
Everyone knows it.

555
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:49,433
朱迪·丹奇都在倒追我呢。
Judy Dench is after me.

556
00:27:49,467 --> 00:27:51,667
朱迪·丹奇迷上你了，
因为……
Judy Dench fancies you,
because...

557
00:27:51,700 --> 00:27:55,133
她为我神魂颠倒，
就因为那次，
显得我特纯爷们儿、特硬汉。
She fancies me like mad,
because of that,
it makes me very butch.

558
00:27:56,100 --> 00:27:58,567
实际上，我们这儿
正好有段视频，
We've got a clip, actually,
here,

559
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:00,633
可以放给大家看看到底怎么回事，
which we can show to you
of what we're on about

560
00:28:00,667 --> 00:28:03,133
也照顾一下当年
还没看《Top Gear》的观众……
for those of you who weren't
watching Top Gear way back...

561
00:28:03,167 --> 00:28:05,500
来了来了。
Here he goes.

562
00:28:05,533 --> 00:28:07,567
好了，冲出赛道了，
然后……
Okay, we're off the road
and then...

563
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:10,733
差点整台车翻过去。
Nearly roll it over.

564
00:28:10,767 --> 00:28:14,433
说真的，
我们其实见过更壮观的
冲出赛道名场面。
I mean, seriously,
we've had some even more
spectacular offs.

565
00:28:14,467 --> 00:28:16,500
我记得那是
《Top Gear》史上第四期节目吧。
I think that was
the fourth ever Top Gear.

566
00:28:16,533 --> 00:28:19,033
我们当时还想：“完了，我们刚把
《歌唱神探》给弄死了。”
We thought, "We've just killed
the Singing Detective."

567
00:28:19,067 --> 00:28:21,367
可不是嘛，
早该有人把他干掉了。
I know,
about time someone killed him.

568
00:28:21,367 --> 00:28:23,667
当然了，从那之后
你就去演《哈利·波特》了。
Of course, since then
Harry Potter's come along.

569
00:28:23,700 --> 00:28:24,933
对啊，我演邓布利多。
Yeah, I'm Dumbledore.

570
00:28:24,967 --> 00:28:27,567
理查德·哈里斯演了两部，
然后他就去世了。
Richard Harris did two films,
then he died.

571
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:29,500
我现在都在演第三部了。
I'm now on my third.

572
00:28:29,533 --> 00:28:33,533
你到底能不能搞懂
《哈利·波特》里台词
一星半点的意思？
Do you understand
the first thing that's been
said in Harry Potter?

573
00:28:33,567 --> 00:28:36,933
我读剧本、
背台词，
我也尽量去理解啊。
I read the script
and learn the lines
and I try to understand it.

574
00:28:36,967 --> 00:28:40,100
我总得搞懂吧，
不是吗？差不多懂吧。（嗤笑）
I have to understand it,
don't I? Sort of. (SCOFFS)

575
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:46,033
经常是我演别的电影时，
压根不知道
到底在演些啥。
Quite often I don't know
what's going on
in other films I do.

576
00:28:46,067 --> 00:28:48,367
比如《夹心蛋糕》，
你知道那部戏
演的是什么吗？
Such as, Layer Cake,
did you know
what was going on in that?

577
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,933
-完全没概念。
-真的假的？
-No idea.
-Really?

578
00:28:49,967 --> 00:28:51,633
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

579
00:28:51,667 --> 00:28:54,600
还有后来我拍
《高斯福庄园》的时候，
And then when I did
Gosford Park,

580
00:28:54,633 --> 00:28:58,467
我得承认，开拍前
我根本连剧本都没翻过。
I must admit I hadn't read it
before I started shooting.

581
00:28:58,500 --> 00:29:01,767
第一天在餐桌旁坐下，
身边坐着玛吉·史密斯
I sat down on the first day
at the dinner table
with Maggie Smith

582
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:03,067
和全体演员，我心想：
and the whole cast
and I thought.

583
00:29:03,100 --> 00:29:05,367
“我压根不知道
在搞些什么名堂！”
"I don't know
what's going on!"

584
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:07,700
我还以为我戏里的老婆
是玛吉·史密斯演的。
I thought my wife was
Maggie Smith.

585
00:29:07,733 --> 00:29:08,833
结果根本不是。
But it wasn't.

586
00:29:10,533 --> 00:29:13,600
结果整场戏下来，
我一直在冲她挤眉弄眼送秋波，
And all through the scene,
I was making eyes at her

587
00:29:13,633 --> 00:29:15,367
她直接问我：
“你看谁呢你？”
and she said,
"Who are you looking at?"

588
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:18,200
-想必你现在还演话剧吧？
-演啊，话剧我还演。
-You still do plays,
presumably?
-I do plays.

589
00:29:18,233 --> 00:29:20,500
今年我演了
职业生涯最棒的一部话剧。
This year I'm doing
my best play ever.

590
00:29:20,533 --> 00:29:24,667
是萨缪尔·贝克特写的，
全长就半小时。
It's a play by Samuel Beckett
and it's half an hour long.

591
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:26,700
是不是绝了？
而且我一句词都没有。
Isn't that brilliant?
And I don't speak.

592
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:31,133
全程只有录音机里
放出来的一个声音，
There's one voice going
on a tape recorder
all through it,

593
00:29:31,167 --> 00:29:32,800
是佩内洛普·威尔顿配的。
that's Penelope Wilton.

594
00:29:32,833 --> 00:29:35,733
那都是提前录好的，
所以我只要一个人
坐在那儿听就行。
That's recorded,
so I sit there
by myself and listen.

595
00:29:35,767 --> 00:29:37,933
-你坐在一张……
-我坐在一张床上。
-You sit on a...
-I sit on a bed.

596
00:29:37,967 --> 00:29:39,633
-就你一个人？
-就我一个。
-All by yourself?
-By myself.

597
00:29:39,667 --> 00:29:41,767
-坐半个小时，一句话不说？
-还穿着睡衣。
-For half an hour
and don't say anything?
-Wearing pyjamas.

598
00:29:41,800 --> 00:29:43,100
这玩意儿还真有人买票来看？
Do people come and see this?

599
00:29:43,133 --> 00:29:45,667
人家都觉得这是有史以来
最伟大的剧作呢。
They reckon it's the greatest
play ever written.

600
00:29:47,567 --> 00:29:50,367
（结巴）怎么可能？你……
那你总得做出点反应吧？
(STAMMERS) How? You?
Do you have to react then?

601
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:55,167
当时有一台摄像机
把我的脸投射在
一张30英尺高的纱幕上。
Well, there's a video camera
projecting my face
onto a scrim, 30 foot high.

602
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:59,867
镜头分九个阶段推进，
越来越近，越来越近。
It comes in in nine stages.
Closer and closer.

603
00:29:59,900 --> 00:30:04,233
我的脸动都不能动，
稍微动一下
看着就跟爆炸了似的。
I can't move my face
or it will look like
an explosion.

604
00:30:05,233 --> 00:30:07,933
我必须保持一动不动。
I must keep very still.

605
00:30:07,967 --> 00:30:09,300
然后在不动的前提下演戏？
And then act without moving?

606
00:30:09,300 --> 00:30:09,367
然后在不动的前提下演戏？
还得同时演戏，
太难了。
And then act without moving?
And act at the same time.
It's very difficult.

607
00:30:09,367 --> 00:30:10,867
还得同时演戏，
太难了。
And act at the same time.
It's very difficult.

608
00:30:10,900 --> 00:30:12,133
不许说话也不许动。
Without talking or moving.

609
00:30:12,167 --> 00:30:15,267
不许说话也不许动，
这确实难。
Without talking or moving.
That's hard.

610
00:30:15,300 --> 00:30:18,033
- 所以他们才找我来演他。
- （全场大笑）
-That's why they
got me for him.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

611
00:30:18,067 --> 00:30:20,133
你能一动不动地
演出心虚的样子吗？
Can you look guilty
without moving?

612
00:30:20,167 --> 00:30:21,333
- 我能演心虚？
- 对，心虚。
-Can I look guilty?
-Yeah, guilty.

613
00:30:21,367 --> 00:30:22,800
我平时看着就一直挺心虚的。
I look guilty all the time.

614
00:30:22,833 --> 00:30:24,467
- 呃……
- （全场大笑）
-Erm...
-(ALL LAUGHING)

615
00:30:24,500 --> 00:30:26,300
讲真，
前几天我也试着演了回戏，
I must say,
I tried acting the other day

616
00:30:26,333 --> 00:30:28,200
拍一个以后要上映的东西。
for something
which is coming out later.

617
00:30:28,233 --> 00:30:30,667
- 我能演愤怒，演愤怒对我来说太容易了。
- 那个确实容易。
-I could do angry.
I find angry very easy.
-That's easy.

618
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:33,100
然后他们问我：
“你能表现得温情点吗？”
Then they said,
"Can you be tender?"

619
00:30:33,133 --> 00:30:35,333
- “不能。”
- （全场大笑）
-"No."
-(ALL LAUGHING)

620
00:30:35,367 --> 00:30:36,967
- 邦德呢。
- 我能演邦德。
-Bond.
-I could be Bond.

621
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,400
你当年差点真成了邦德！
You were going to be Bond!

622
00:30:38,433 --> 00:30:40,667
年轻那会儿，
他们确实就邦德一角面试过我。
Well, I was interviewed
for Bond when I was young.

623
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:42,200
- 卡比·布洛克利面试的？
- 对。
-By Cubby Broccoli?
-Yeah.

624
00:30:42,233 --> 00:30:45,567
我们上了楼，在桌前坐下，
然后我说……我当时就笑了。
We went upstairs
and sat at the table
and I said... I laughed.

625
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:47,400
我说：
“我演不了詹姆斯·邦德。”
他问：“为啥演不了？”
I said,
"I can't be James Bond."
He said, "Why not?"

626
00:30:47,433 --> 00:30:49,800
我说：“我这胸大、双下巴，
还没牙。”
I said "Well, I've got tits
and double chin, no teeth."

627
00:30:49,833 --> 00:30:51,367
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

628
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:54,167
“还是个秃顶。”
他说：“害，
肖恩·康纳利不也这样嘛。”
"And a bald head."
He said, "Oh,
so has Sean Connery."

629
00:30:55,733 --> 00:30:56,833
呃，这……
Well, it's...

630
00:30:57,467 --> 00:30:59,200
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

631
00:30:59,233 --> 00:31:00,933
我问：“那你怎么掩盖那胸呢？”
I said, "How would you
cover the tits?"

632
00:31:00,967 --> 00:31:03,233
他说：“我们就拿装满冰块的皮袋子
往上一捂。
He said, "We'd just
put the leather bags,
full of ice on there.

633
00:31:03,267 --> 00:31:06,167
“就在开拍之前捂上，
然后就……”
（发出滋滋声）
"Just before the take.
They go..."
(MAKES SIZZLING SOUND)

634
00:31:07,233 --> 00:31:09,567
怎么着，按你的说法，
肖恩·康纳利是个女人？！
What, Sean Connery
you're saying, is a woman?

635
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,500
反正是别人跟我这么说的。
Well, that's what I was told.

636
00:31:11,533 --> 00:31:13,033
我是说，咱们摸着良心讲，
I mean, let's be honest.

637
00:31:13,067 --> 00:31:15,867
你接受采访时
满嘴跑火车
其实是相当出名的。
You are actually
quite famous, for making
stuff up in interviews.

638
00:31:15,900 --> 00:31:17,367
- 编故事嘛。
- 对啊。
-Stories.
-Yeah.

639
00:31:17,367 --> 00:31:19,467
这没办法啊，
我讨厌接受采访。
Well, you have to.
I hate interviews.

640
00:31:19,500 --> 00:31:21,033
哦，天呐，抱歉。
Oh, God. Sorry.

641
00:31:21,067 --> 00:31:24,400
反正我看了，惨不忍睹，
所以我干脆满嘴跑火车。
Well, I do, and it's awful,
so I just tell lies.

642
00:31:27,767 --> 00:31:30,900
所以要是有人……
我知道你曾经跟一个记者吹过，
So if someone...
I know you did
once tell an interviewer

643
00:31:30,933 --> 00:31:32,667
说你是英国皇家芭蕾舞团的成员。
you were a member
of the Royal Ballet.

644
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:36,000
对，我说我以前是
皇家芭蕾舞团的芭蕾舞演员。
Yeah, I said
I was a ballet dancer
at Royal Ballet.

645
00:31:36,033 --> 00:31:38,800
-你们笑什么？
-（全场大笑）
-What are you laughing at?
-(ALL LAUGHING)

646
00:31:38,833 --> 00:31:41,067
然后那记者问：
“那你后来怎么不跳了呢？”
And he said,
"Why did you give it up?"

647
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:44,267
我说：“我在歌剧院的舞台上一脚踩空摔下去了，
I said, "I fell off
the stage at the opera house

648
00:31:44,367 --> 00:31:46,000
“直接砸穿了一个定音鼓。”
"and went through
a kettle drum."

649
00:31:46,033 --> 00:31:47,800
（嘎嘎怪笑）
(CACKLES)

650
00:31:47,833 --> 00:31:49,767
后来你还跟另一个人说你是同性恋。
Then you said to someone else
you were gay.

651
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:51,400
没错，我说我是同性恋。
Yes. I said I was gay.

652
00:31:51,433 --> 00:31:54,500
那人说：
“你演过奥斯卡……”
我演过奥斯卡·王尔德嘛。
The man said,
"You played Oscar..."
I played Oscar Wilde.

653
00:31:54,533 --> 00:31:57,567
他说：
“你觉得演这角色难吗？”
我说：“一点都不难。”
He said,
"Did you find that difficult?"
I said, "No, I didn't."

654
00:31:57,600 --> 00:32:00,200
他又问：“那关于
同性恋这部分呢？”
He said, "What about
the homosexuality?"

655
00:32:00,233 --> 00:32:02,033
这问题可把我惹烦了，你懂吧？
于是我说：
So that annoyed me, you know?
And I said,

656
00:32:02,067 --> 00:32:05,467
“哎呀，我觉得这简直小菜一碟，
因为我以前就是个同性恋。”
"Well, I found that very easy
because I used to be
a homosexual."

657
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:06,833
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

658
00:32:10,100 --> 00:32:12,667
而且那记者脑子特别缺心眼，你知道吧。
And he was so thick, you know.

659
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:14,833
我接着说：“但我后来被迫放弃了。”
I said, "But I was
forced to give it up."

660
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,133
然后他就真顺着问了。
And then
he asked the question.

661
00:32:20,167 --> 00:32:22,767
他问：“噢，那是为什么呢？
为什么放弃了？”
He said, "Oh, why was that?
Why was that?"

662
00:32:22,800 --> 00:32:25,033
我说：“因为搞得我直流眼泪。”
I said, "Because it made
my eyes water."

663
00:32:25,067 --> 00:32:26,533
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

664
00:32:27,933 --> 00:32:29,367
真事儿！
It's true.

665
00:32:31,100 --> 00:32:33,367
我本来以为他会笑，结果他根本没笑。
And I thought he'd laugh,
but he didn't.

666
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:34,867
-他整个人都……
-他居然还一笔一划记下来了！
-He's so...
-He wrote it down.

667
00:32:38,633 --> 00:32:41,367
还有那种电影巡回宣传采访，
There are those press junkets
as well when you go round,

668
00:32:41,367 --> 00:32:43,400
绝对是个瞎编胡扯的绝佳机会，
telling there's a marvellous
opportunity to lie,

669
00:32:43,433 --> 00:32:45,933
-每当有新片上映的时候。
-对。
-when they launch a film.
-Yeah.

670
00:32:45,967 --> 00:32:48,467
-演员们得四处赶场……
-这种事我干过可多了。
-Actors have to move around...
-I've done a lot of that.

671
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:51,733
每隔十分钟就得面对摄像机
接受一次采访，
You get an interview
every 10 minutes
with a video camera

672
00:32:51,767 --> 00:32:54,367
各路记者在某家高档酒店的门外排起长队。
and they queue up outside
the door in some posh hotel.

673
00:32:54,367 --> 00:32:58,700
但我们这些演员进场前，
都会互相给对方出任务。
But all us, actors,
before we do it,
give each other tasks.

674
00:32:58,733 --> 00:33:01,267
当年拍《断头谷》的时候我领到的一个任务，
And one of my tasks
on Sleepy Hollow,

675
00:33:01,367 --> 00:33:02,500
约翰尼·德普跟我说，
Johnny Depp told me

676
00:33:02,533 --> 00:33:04,433
我必须把“克劳迪娅·雪佛的小内裤”
I had to get
Claudia Schiffer's knickers

677
00:33:04,467 --> 00:33:06,833
塞进我对每一个问题的回答里。
into my reply
for each question.

678
00:33:06,867 --> 00:33:08,133
-每一个……
-每一个问题。
-Every...
-Every question.

679
00:33:08,167 --> 00:33:09,900
-每一个问题都要带上！
-（全场大笑）
-Every question!
-(ALL LAUGHING)

680
00:33:11,967 --> 00:33:13,567
-你搞定了吗？
-小菜一碟。
-Did you manage it?
-Easy.

681
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:14,867
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

682
00:33:18,033 --> 00:33:19,467
当然，最妙的是，
Now the great thing is,
of course,

683
00:33:19,500 --> 00:33:21,467
你当年其实是正经学工程出身的，对吧？
is that you actually trained
as an engineer, didn't you?

684
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:22,967
没错，是的。
Yeah, yeah.

685
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,667
-那算是你的初恋了。
-对，是我的激情所在！
-That's your sort
of first love.
-Yeah, my passion!

686
00:33:24,700 --> 00:33:27,000
-你知道我们今天搞来的那台Prodrive吧？
-知道。
-You know that Prodrive
we've got today?
-Yeah.

687
00:33:27,033 --> 00:33:29,800
-你懂这有什么区别吗？
-当然，谁都知道。
-Do you understand
there's a difference?
-Of course, everyone does.

688
00:33:29,833 --> 00:33:31,167
-你才不懂呢。
-我懂啊。
-You don't.
-Yes.

689
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:33,367
不就是两个齿轮在那转嘛。
It's just two cogs rotating.

690
00:33:33,367 --> 00:33:34,767
一个轮子转得比另一个快。
One wheel goes faster
than the other.

691
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:37,800
-对，我知道。
-但这台里面装了电子系统，不是吗？
-Yes, I know.
-But this has electronics
inside, doesn't it?

692
00:33:37,833 --> 00:33:40,267
他才应该来当主持人。
He should be a presenter.

693
00:33:40,367 --> 00:33:42,033
我真纳闷你怎么当上这节目主持人的，
I'm surprised
you're presenting
this programme

694
00:33:42,067 --> 00:33:44,000
居然连Prodrive都搞不明白。
and you don't know
about the Prodrive.

695
00:33:44,033 --> 00:33:45,800
我哪知道它是怎么运作的！
I don't know how it works!

696
00:33:45,833 --> 00:33:47,367
说了你得吓一跳。
You'd be astonished.

697
00:33:47,367 --> 00:33:49,267
-我知道，我真的知道……
-在场的所有人都懂。
-I do know, I do know...
-Everyone here does.

698
00:33:49,367 --> 00:33:50,767
-不，我……
-（观众大笑）
-No, I'm...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

699
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:53,000
-好吧，那我们还是聊车吧。
-行啊。
-Okay, well,
we'll talk about cars then.
-Yeah.

700
00:33:53,033 --> 00:33:54,800
你可以给我们对比一下。
You can give us a comparison.

701
00:33:54,833 --> 00:33:57,167
咱们这台新车跟老车比起来怎么样？
How is our new car
compared to our old one?

702
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:58,833
噢，我觉得开起来更容易了。
Oh, I think,
it's easier to drive.

703
00:33:58,867 --> 00:33:59,967
-真的？
-真的。
-Really?
-Yeah.

704
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,667
行，我们马上就能见分晓了。
Well, we're gonna
find out now.

705
00:34:01,700 --> 00:34:03,767
（低语）天呐，求求了，千万别放这段。
(WHISPERS) Oh, God, please,
don't show this.

706
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:05,867
（吸鼻子）
(SNIFFLING)

707
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:08,400
谁想看迈克尔练习的片段？
Who'd like to see Michael
having a practise?

708
00:34:08,433 --> 00:34:10,233
-没人想看。
-观众：想看！
-No one.
-AUDIENCE: Yes!

709
00:34:10,267 --> 00:34:13,367
我们来看看。
来瞧一瞧。
Let's have a look at this.
Let's have a look.

710
00:34:13,367 --> 00:34:14,900
迈克尔·甘本：
我们这是开到哪儿了？
MICHAEL GAMBON:
Where are we here?

711
00:34:14,933 --> 00:34:16,367
看起来像是倒数第二个弯。
It looks like
second-to-last corner.

712
00:34:16,367 --> 00:34:17,933
克拉克森：
没错，就是倒数第二个弯。
CLARKSON:
Yes, it is, second to last.

713
00:34:17,967 --> 00:34:20,367
就在“甘本弯”前面！
Just before Gambon!

714
00:34:20,367 --> 00:34:22,867
我当时吓坏了。看看那个可怜的老头子。
I was so frightened.
Look at that poor old man.

715
00:34:22,900 --> 00:34:24,367
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

716
00:34:27,367 --> 00:34:29,400
大家准备好
看完整的一圈了吗？
Are we ready
to see the full lap now?

717
00:34:29,433 --> 00:34:31,667
-观众：准备好了！
-放录像！
-AUDIENCE: Yes!
-Play the tape.

718
00:34:31,700 --> 00:34:32,800
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINE REVS)

719
00:34:33,367 --> 00:34:35,533
（轮胎尖叫）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

720
00:34:35,567 --> 00:34:38,133
-克拉克森：
这起步可真够暴躁的。
-（引擎咆哮）
-CLARKSON:
That was an aggressive start.
-(ENGINE ROARS)

721
00:34:38,167 --> 00:34:41,133
噢，这档位总能在里面找着的。
挂上了。
Ooh, there's one
in there somewhere.
You got it.

722
00:34:41,167 --> 00:34:43,267
冒昧问一句，
你今年高寿了？
How old are you now,
if that's not a rude question?

723
00:34:43,367 --> 00:34:45,467
- 二十八。
- 二十八？
-Twenty-eight.
-Twenty-eight?

724
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:46,867
克拉克森：真敢说。
好吧，现在这是……
CLARKSON: Clear.
Well, that's now...

725
00:34:46,900 --> 00:34:48,667
呃，其实这一下是切弯了，
Well, that was actually
cutting that corner

726
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:52,467
但看在那块儿路面滑的份上，
我就放你一马。
but since it's slippery
through that I'll let you off.

727
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:54,667
依我看，
这开法还挺悠闲的。
A relaxed driving style,
I would say.

728
00:34:54,700 --> 00:34:56,267
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

729
00:34:56,367 --> 00:34:58,233
但也够猛。速度真快。
But aggressive. That's quick.

730
00:35:01,367 --> 00:35:04,067
进入“锤头弯”。
这回可没切弯。
And into the Hammerhead.
Not cutting this one.

731
00:35:04,100 --> 00:35:05,533
（轮胎尖叫声）
(SCREECHING)

732
00:35:05,567 --> 00:35:07,400
要撞死摄像师了。
没撞着，他拔腿跑了。
Gonna kill the cameraman.
No, he's running away.

733
00:35:07,433 --> 00:35:08,700
那还行。
That's all right.

734
00:35:08,733 --> 00:35:10,700
天呐！
God!

735
00:35:10,733 --> 00:35:12,867
这里就是斯提格……
他是不是让你全油门冲过去？
This is where Stig...
Did he tell you
to go flat out?

736
00:35:12,900 --> 00:35:14,700
甘本：是啊，你看。
GAMBON: Yeah. Look.

737
00:35:14,733 --> 00:35:17,267
- 克拉克森：你在这儿真是全油门踩到底？
- 是啊。
-CLARKSON : And you are doing
flat out through here?
-Yeah.

738
00:35:17,367 --> 00:35:19,200
- （呼啸声）
- 克拉克森：芜湖！
-(ZOOMING)
-CLARKSON : Whoo!

739
00:35:20,167 --> 00:35:22,067
把摄像机都带歪了。
Moved the camera.

740
00:35:22,100 --> 00:35:24,933
拉近镜头。来了来了，
各位，他正逼近“甘本弯”！
Closer. Here we go,
he's coming up
to Gambon, everybody!

741
00:35:24,967 --> 00:35:26,867
以你命名的专属弯道！
Your own corner!

742
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:29,000
他直接横着甩过去了！
He's gone right around!

743
00:35:29,033 --> 00:35:30,533
冲线！
Across the line!

744
00:35:30,567 --> 00:35:32,667
（观众欢呼与掌声）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING
AND APPLAUDING)

745
00:35:36,367 --> 00:35:37,833
克拉克森：这可真是……
CLARKSON: It is...

746
00:35:42,367 --> 00:35:43,967
那个弯道到底惹你什么了？
What is it with that corner?

747
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,900
不知道。
我就是看它不顺眼。
I don't know.
I just don't like it.

748
00:35:45,933 --> 00:35:47,833
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

749
00:35:47,867 --> 00:35:51,700
言归正传，上次你开铃木Liana，成绩是1分55秒。
Anyway, last time you were
here in the Liana. 1:55.

750
00:35:51,733 --> 00:35:53,100
惨不忍睹。
Terrible.

751
00:35:53,133 --> 00:35:56,267
这次你开的是Lacetti，
You did it in the Lacetti,

752
00:35:56,367 --> 00:35:58,733
成绩是1分……
in one minute...

753
00:35:58,767 --> 00:36:01,967
鉴于BBC独特奇葩的资金运作方式，
Due to the unique way
the BBC is funded,

754
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,433
这破笔写不出字来。
the pen doesn't work.

755
00:36:07,900 --> 00:36:10,767
正好烘托紧张气氛。
不不不！我搞得定。
That increases the tension.
No, no, no! I shall manage.

756
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:12,400
1分……
One minute...

757
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:15,500
要战胜的目标是55秒，还记得吧？
你上次的成绩。
55 to beat, remember?
Your last time.

758
00:36:15,533 --> 00:36:17,167
50秒3！
50.3!

759
00:36:17,200 --> 00:36:19,100
所以，成绩揭晓了，
女士们，先生们！
So, there we are,
ladies and gentlemen!

760
00:36:20,467 --> 00:36:22,733
正好跟……一模一样。
事实上……
Exactly the same as...
In fact...

761
00:36:26,667 --> 00:36:28,867
我今天心情好，
就把你排在他前面吧。
I'm feeling generous.
I'll put you above him.

762
00:36:29,800 --> 00:36:31,233
干得漂亮。
Well done.

763
00:36:35,067 --> 00:36:38,267
那么，女士们先生们——
So, ladies and gentlemen,

764
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:39,933
-迈克尔·甘本！
-噢！
-Michael Gambon!
-Oh!

765
00:36:39,967 --> 00:36:41,400
（观众欢呼与掌声）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING
AND APPLAUDING)

766
00:36:41,433 --> 00:36:42,800
非常感谢您的光临。
Thank you so much for coming.

767
00:36:47,633 --> 00:36:51,900
言归正传，今年我最期待
试驾的那辆车，
Now, the car that I've been
most looking forward
to driving this year

768
00:36:51,933 --> 00:36:53,967
既不是新款法拉利599，
is not the new Ferrari 599

769
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,200
也不是兰博基尼
Gallardo Spyder！
or the Lamborghini
Gallardo Spyder!

770
00:36:56,233 --> 00:36:57,933
不，而是这一台！
No, it's this!

771
00:36:57,967 --> 00:37:00,267
全新雪铁龙C6。
The new Citroen C6.

772
00:37:00,367 --> 00:37:02,233
然而不幸的是，
事实证明，
Unfortunately,
as it turns out,

773
00:37:02,267 --> 00:37:06,100
杰里米也很想开
这台全新的雪铁龙C6。
Jeremy has also been
looking forward to driving
the new Citroen C6.

774
00:37:06,133 --> 00:37:09,200
鉴于……
他块头比我大，
所以他就给抢去开了。
And, well,
he's bigger than me,
so he's done it.

775
00:37:20,133 --> 00:37:22,967
克拉克森：
这就是当年的雪铁龙CX。
CLARKSON:
This is the old Citroen CX.

776
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:25,600
它全身上下都透着疯癫。
And it was mad in every way.

777
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:31,700
音响是竖着装的。
The stereo is vertical.

778
00:37:31,733 --> 00:37:35,467
转向灯开关在这儿，
而且打完还不会自动回弹。
The indicator switch is here
and it doesn't self-cancel.

779
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:37,767
还有这刹车，
用起来就像个开关。
And the brakes work
like a switch.

780
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:39,433
要么像现在这样完全没反应，
They're either off like now

781
00:37:39,467 --> 00:37:41,800
要么一踩就直接……
（怪笑）
or they're on like...
(CACKLES)

782
00:37:47,667 --> 00:37:49,700
想开着这车穿过城镇，
Trying to drive this car
through a town

783
00:37:49,733 --> 00:37:53,833
简直就像戴着拳击手套
去给插头接电线。
was like trying to wire a plug
while wearing boxing gloves.

784
00:37:53,867 --> 00:37:56,567
结局注定是一场悲剧。
It was always going
to end in tears.

785
00:37:57,133 --> 00:37:58,533
噢，忘了打转向灯。
Oh, no indicators.

786
00:38:00,200 --> 00:38:01,733
太棒了，不好意思啊。
Great. Sorry.

787
00:38:03,833 --> 00:38:05,667
哎呀，抱歉。（笑）
Oops, sorry. (LAUGHS)

788
00:38:08,367 --> 00:38:11,067
但你猜怎么着，我超爱它。
But you know what, I loved it.

789
00:38:11,100 --> 00:38:13,467
我爱死这单辐式方向盘了，
I love the one-prong
steering wheel,

790
00:38:13,500 --> 00:38:15,367
爱这软绵绵的座椅，
the softness of the seats,

791
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:18,900
爱这棉花糖一样的悬挂，
还有这巨大无比的空间！
the softness of the suspension
and the space!

792
00:38:18,933 --> 00:38:23,233
这后排空间大得
都足够在里面办一场
小型网球锦标赛了。
There was enough room
back here to stage
a small tennis tournament.

793
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:28,400
CX是如此与众不同，
如此不按常理出牌。
The CX was just so different,
so left-field.

794
00:38:29,500 --> 00:38:31,600
正因如此，六年前我非常难过，
And that's why I was sad
six years ago,

795
00:38:31,633 --> 00:38:36,767
当时雪铁龙宣布
他们将彻底停产
这种又大又疯狂的轿车。
when Citroen announced
that they'd stop making
big insane cars for good.

796
00:38:38,367 --> 00:38:40,233
（雷声轰鸣）
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

797
00:38:41,433 --> 00:38:43,833
但现在，他们杀回来了。
Only now, they're back.

798
00:38:45,867 --> 00:38:48,467
从他们最初设想的设计草图
The original sketches
for what they had in mind

799
00:38:48,500 --> 00:38:52,767
就能看出，这车跟宝马奔驰
那一套循规蹈矩的套路截然不同。
show something
radically different to the BMW
and Mercedes norm.

800
00:38:55,467 --> 00:38:57,667
完全没有一点儿德国味儿。
Something not at all German.

801
00:39:00,900 --> 00:39:02,900
于是最终成果就是它了。
And this is what resulted.

802
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:09,167
相比最初的设计草图，
它确实收敛了不少，
It's been toned down a bit
from those original drawings,

803
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:12,033
但依然保留了四个
无框车门、
but it still has four
pillarless doors,

804
00:39:12,067 --> 00:39:13,967
一块内凹式后挡风玻璃，
a concave rear windscreen,

805
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:18,133
以及能让车子在原地静止时
也能晃荡起伏的悬挂系统。
and suspension
that lets it move about
while it's standing still.

806
00:39:19,367 --> 00:39:21,833
内饰也是同样的调调。
It's the same story
with the interior.

807
00:39:21,867 --> 00:39:25,500
要是你选了米白真皮内饰，
坐进去还挺惬意的。
If you go
for the cream leather,
it's a pleasant place to sit.

808
00:39:26,533 --> 00:39:29,467
浓浓的巴黎味儿，绝非柏林那种死板作风。
Much more Paris than Berlin.

809
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:37,900
这一切确实很棒，
但那股子癫狂劲儿跑哪儿去了？
And that's all very nice
but where is the lunacy?

810
00:39:37,933 --> 00:39:41,600
没错，它配了双层玻璃，
车内极度安静；还有，没错，
Yes, it's got double glazing
so it's very quiet, and yes,

811
00:39:41,633 --> 00:39:45,367
它有抬头显示；还有，没错，
座椅上还带个功能，
it's got a head-up display,
and yes,
there's a feature in the seat

812
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:49,133
只要我压过车道白线，
它就会嗡嗡震动。
that vibrates if I stray
over the white lines.

813
00:39:49,167 --> 00:39:51,833
这功能对单身汉来说
倒是个福音。
Which is nice
if you're a bachelor.

814
00:39:53,667 --> 00:39:58,733
可我想要的是一种
跟世上任何车都截然不同的感觉。
But I want it to feel
completely different
to any other car.

815
00:39:58,767 --> 00:40:03,167
我想启动它，
得靠去舔方向盘上的这块面板。
I want to start it
by licking a panel here
on the steering wheel.

816
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:05,933
我想让换挡杆用大黄茎做成，
I want the gear lever
to be made from rhubarb

817
00:40:05,967 --> 00:40:07,800
还得直接从遮阳板里戳出来。
and just stick
out of the sun visor.

818
00:40:07,833 --> 00:40:12,433
我想感觉自己仿佛掉进了达利的画作里，
周围一切都在融化！
I want to feel like I'm in
a Salvador Dali painting
and it's all melting.

819
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:18,700
那它实际表现究竟如何呢？
So how does it stack up?

820
00:40:18,733 --> 00:40:20,367
这是转向灯吗？
Is this an indicator?

821
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:22,400
还真是。这根本不对！
Yes, it is. It shouldn't be.

822
00:40:24,233 --> 00:40:25,633
这儿本该是
后备箱开启按键。
That should be
the boot release.

823
00:40:25,667 --> 00:40:29,867
转向灯应该藏在
这附近的某个角落里才对。
全都搞错了！
The indicator should be
in here somewhere.
It's all wrong!

824
00:40:29,900 --> 00:40:31,633
全错！全错！荒谬透顶！
Wrong, wrong, wrong!

825
00:40:34,100 --> 00:40:35,833
作为一辆车，
它也太循规蹈矩了。
As a car,
it's conventional too.

826
00:40:35,867 --> 00:40:39,767
它是前轮驱动，
而不是“侧轮驱动”。
It's front-wheel drive,
rather than side-wheel drive.

827
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:42,900
起售价是两万九千五百英镑，
And prices start at £29,500

828
00:40:42,933 --> 00:40:45,900
而不是两万九千五百个扎格星币。
rather than 29,500 zargs.

829
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:53,067
方向盘居然是圆的。
The steering wheel
is circular.

830
00:40:53,100 --> 00:40:54,967
座椅硬得像德国车，
The seats are German-hard

831
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:57,533
后排空间虽说塞得下我，
and while there is enough
space in the back for me,

832
00:40:57,567 --> 00:41:00,133
但还远没宽敞到能在里面遛狗。
there isn't enough
to take a dog for a walk.

833
00:41:00,167 --> 00:41:04,133
而坐在一辆雪铁龙大旗舰后排，
你理应能遛狗！本该如此！
And you should be able
to do that in the back
of a big Citroen. You should!

834
00:41:05,767 --> 00:41:09,800
所以眼下看来，
这帮“吃奶酪的投降猴子”，
So it's beginning to look
like the cheese-eating
surrender monkeys

835
00:41:09,833 --> 00:41:11,500
这次是彻底怂了。
have bottled it.

836
00:41:14,167 --> 00:41:18,500
现在我们要说到
最让人大失所望的一点了。
And now we get to the
most disappointing thing
of them all.

837
